# REQUIRES: verilator
# Multicycle evaluation (--stage-levels N --multicycle <class>): a deep class
# evaluates one instance at a time over M host cycles, M its cone's estimated
# levels over N, with no stage registers: its state and inputs taken into
# capture registers at the read, the logic over M host cycles into end
# registers a position before the state pass, which writes from them. The
# leaves (Driver/Inputs/deep_mc: an oldest-first scan whose result picks the
# address of two registered reads, a RAM write and an element write; a late
# link into the second leaf) against the target (tb_late.sv), from zero
# state, with bubbles and stalled channels: one copy at N = 6 and 4, two
# copies, a copy per instance, paged state (byte masks, and a dense page
# word), nested sequencers with a short lead, the link kinds, and a span of 2.
# The simulator checks on every run that each evaluation's capture and end
# registers are at least M host cycles apart and no other capture falls
# between (the timing its constraints assume).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/deep_mc
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/plain --static --bubbles Leaf > %t/plain.log 2>&1
# RUN: foldsim-opt %t/plain/foldsim_sim.mlir --pass-pipeline='builtin.module(beacon-estimate-timing{top=Leaf_static report=-})' -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEEP
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/m6 --static --bubbles --stage-levels 6 --multicycle Leaf Leaf > %t/m6.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=M6 < %t/m6.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=XDC < %t/m6/foldsim_multicycle.xdc
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JSON < %t/m6/foldsim_sim.json
# RUN: foldsim-opt %t/m6/foldsim_sim.mlir --pass-pipeline='builtin.module(beacon-estimate-timing{top=Leaf_static output=%t/m6/ep.csv report=-})' -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RAW6
# RUN: python3 %S/../../tools/foldsim/foldsim_mc_judge.py %t/m6/ep.csv %t/m6/foldsim_sim.json --min-levels 7 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JUDGE6
